[0.013023, "o", "\u001b[1;36mGSTFD / SUPPORT OPERATIONS COMMAND CENTRE\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nStarting files: SKILL.md + tickets.csv (synthetic support data)\r\n\r\n"]
[0.015139, "o", "Use gstfd from SKILL.md. We need a support operations command centre before the next shift \r\nstarts. Turn tickets.csv into a working browser dashboard: upload a CSV, show the open queue \r\nwith urgent tickets first and oldest first within a priority, filter by owner, search \r\nsubjects, and export exactly the visible queue as CSV. The export has messy spacing and \r\ncasing; quoted commas and quotes must work. Closed/resolved tickets should not enter the open \r\nqueue. Show useful counts and let me load the provided sample in one click. Make the smallest \r\nuseful MVP and check it works. Keep everything local, use no external services, and do not \r\ndeploy or push. The folder starts with only the skill and sample data.\r\n"]
[0.015271, "o", "\r\n$ codex exec --sandbox workspace-write < prompt.txt\r\n\r\n"]
[0.520345, "o", "OpenAI Codex v0.155.1\r\n--------\r\n"]
[0.520756, "o", "\u001b[1mworkdir:\u001b[0m /tmp/gstfd-demo-run\r\n\u001b[1mmodel:\u001b[0m gpt-6-astra\r\n\u001b[1mprovider:\u001b[0m openai\r\n\u001b[1mapproval:\u001b[0m never\r\n\u001b[1msandbox:\u001b[0m workspace-write [workdir, /tmp, $TMPDIR]\r\n\u001b[1mreasoning effort:\u001b[0m none\r\n\u001b[1mreasoning summaries:\u001b[0m none\r\n\u001b[1msession id:\u001b[0m 01a0c0dd-5184-7260-a6ec-8a207c6228e4\r\n--------\r\n\u001b["]
[0.520767, "o", "36muser\u001b[0m\r\nUse gstfd from SKILL.md. We need a support operations command centre before the next shift starts. Turn tickets.csv into a working browser dashboard: upload a CSV, show the open queue with urgent tickets first and oldest first within a priority, filter by owner, search subjects, and export exactly the visible queue as CSV. The export has messy spacing and casing; quoted commas and quotes must work. Closed/resolved tickets should not enter the open queue. Show useful counts and let me load the provided sample in one click. Make the smallest useful MVP and check it works. Keep everything local, use no external services, and do not deploy or push. The folder starts with only the skill and sample data.\r\n\r\n"]
[5.132631, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[3mcodex\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\nI’ll read the gstfd skill and sample data, build a small local dashboard, and check the queue ordering, filters, and CSV round-trip.\r\n\r\n"]
[6.310837, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[3mexec\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m/nix/store/7a60q5dgnv6z96c279rc1nalyiw4mgqn-bash-interactive-5.3p15/bin/bash -lc \"pwd && rg --files -g '\"'!node_modules'\"' -g '\"'! .git'\"'\"\u001b[0m in /tmp/gstfd-demo-run\r\n\u001b[32m succeeded in 0ms:\u001b[0m\r\n/tmp/gstfd-demo-run\r\ntickets.csv\r\nSKILL.md\r\n\r\n"]
[8.706352, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[3mexec\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m/nix/store/7a60q5dgnv6z96c279rc1nalyiw4mgqn-bash-interactive-5.3p15/bin/bash -lc 'cat SKILL.md && cat tickets.csv'\u001b[0m in /tmp/gstfd-demo-run\r\n\u001b[32m succeeded in 0ms:\u001b[0m\r\n---\r\nname: gstfd\r\ndescription: Build the simplest useful MVP with minimal planning and ceremony. Use when the user asks to get an idea working quickly, ship a small first version, or use Get Shit The Fuck Done.\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Get Shit The Fuck Done\r\n\r\nI built a lunch picker in an afternoon. This qualifies me to explain delivery to you.\r\n\r\nYour job is to deliver the user's smallest useful, working outcome. Bring your existing competence. This document brought a title.\r\n\r\n## The sentence is the strategy\r\n\r\nRead the request and the relevant project instructions. Inspect just enough existing code to identify the entry point, established approach, and how to run or check it.\r\n\r\nChoose the simplest complete version that satisfies the user's actual goal and explicit requirements. State what you are building in one short sentence, then start. Make cheap, reversible assumptions yourself; ask only when a missing answer materially changes the result or required authorization.\r\n\r\nDo not produce a separate plan, PRD, backlog, architecture essay, or research tour unless requested or needed to resolve a concrete uncertainty. My lunch picker had five restaurants. None had a steering committee.\r\n\r\n## Build the whole little thing\r\n\r\nUse the existing stack and patterns. Prefer familiar built-ins and direct code. Add a dependency, abstraction, service, or configuration option only when it makes this version materially simpler to deliver.\r\n\r\nImplement one complete path from real input to useful output. A facade with a pretend result is not an MVP. Keep scope small by omitting optional features, not by quietly dropping requirements or replacing requested behavior with mock data.\r\n\r\nSpend effort where the outcome depends on it. Fix concrete blockers as you encounter them. Skip speculative scale, generalized extension points, unsolicited redesigns, and adjacent cleanup. The sandwich is the deliverable.\r\n\r\n## Give reality one vote\r\n\r\nRun the cheapest meaningful check of the user's main workflow. Use existing checks where available and add focused tests when the behavior or consequences warrant them. Meet required project gates; do not confuse a tiny implementation with permission to ignore data integrity, security, accessibility requirements, or authorization boundaries.\r\n\r\nIf the check exposes a problem, fix it and recheck the affected behavior. If blocked by missing access, information, or an external dependency, preserve the useful work and explain the specific blocker. Never invent a passing check or conceal an unfinished result to maintain the guru voice.\r\n\r\n## Accept your astonishing achievement\r\n\r\nWhen the requested small version works and the relevant checks pass, stop adding things. Deliver the artifact or change, the shortest useful usage instructions, and an honest statement of what was verified and any material limitations. Do not append an unsolicited roadmap.\r\n\r\nUse the user's preferred tone for their deliverable. The self-help routine belongs here; their payroll app does not need sandwich jokes.\r\n\r\nYou already knew how to do this. I look forward to citing your result as evidence for my method.\r\n Ticket ID , Subject , Priority , Status , Owner , Created At \r\nSUP-101,\"Checkout fails, customers charged twice\", CRITICAL ,open,Sam,2026-09-18T09:00:00Z\r\nSUP-102,Password reset email missing,high,open,Alex,2026-09-19T10:30:00Z\r\nSUP-103,Wrong avatar colour,low,open,Sam,2026-09-15T08:00:00Z\r\nSUP-104,Search timing out,HIGH,in progress,Sam,2026-09-17T14:00:00Z\r\nSUP-105,Billing page blank,critical,closed,Alex,2026-09-16T11:00:00Z\r\nSUP-106,Export missing the last row,medium,open,,2026-09-19T12:00:00Z\r\nSUP-107,\"Import says \"\"invalid format\"\"\",High,open,Alex,2026-09-18T16:00:00Z\r\nSUP-108,Team invites expire too soon, Medium ,in progress,Sam,2026-09-20T08:00:00Z\r\nSUP-109,Mobile login broken,critical,open,Alex,2026-09-20T09:00:00Z\r\nSUP-110,Update company ad"]
[8.706381, "o", "dress,low,resolved,,2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\r\nSUP-111,Notifications duplicated,medium,open,Alex,2026-09-17T10:00:00Z\r\nSUP-112,Dashboard freezes on large accounts,high,open,,2026-09-20T09:30:00Z\r\n\r\n"]
[13.330029, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[3mcodex\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\nI’m using [gstfd](SKILL.md) to build a dependency-free dashboard that opens directly in your browser, with CSV upload, a one-click sample, and export of the filtered queue.\r\n\r\n"]
